All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (5 tracked passages; probe 3% / 18%; the two capacity-failed lanes were relaunched and ran); plan / canon / protected-text audit (REPAIR, bounded; thirty-seven exact fixes; all thirteen author flags KEPT). **Seventeen applied by the coordinator**: the sixteen marker restorations and the light. **Four AMENDED to the plan's own pieces** where the source's fuller wording clashed with this edition (Cleon's speech uses a term the edition never has; the leaf's aside contradicts the live first reading; the title sentence would have doubled *The Architect*; Seln's speech put the case on his back for four years against closed chapter 18's chest and twelve). **Twenty DECLINED**: fix 17, and fixes 18–36 as a class (the audit read "does not turn unbidden until Millrace" as forbidding the outward lean that the same packet prescribes). The editorial read's "marked, not read" objection to the chronicle is DECLINED (the line is protected text that must stand once; the hole is what is not read). Speakers the author's staging had left open and the audit pinned: the cups line is Cael's; both street lines are Seln's; "there" is Cleon's. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author** (thirteen joins, five tracked chains, two orientation cues).

