editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-04.md:127:Anchor asked it of the plate under the axle, in its thin held note, as it had asked at every sill and gate since Ostrand. For once the question had a great deal to be said for it. He had laid a point on a slab in a drowned hall, and nothing that lived under that floor had been able to tip the stone while he held it; a point laid here would hold a lip of ice in the same way.
