editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-04.md-146-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-04.md:147:There was no grey on him. He hauled left-handed, lying on his face, with his boots dug into the snow for all the purchase that he had; and a drowned sheepskin with a man inside it came up over the lip, an inch at a time, and slid out onto the ice like a seal. The carter lay and coughed water.
