editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-188-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-189-He showed them as they walked. A flat hand, with the palm to the ground, was *stand*: wherever a person was, and as he was. A shut fist was *seen*, and one looked where the fist went and did not ask. Two fingers lifted were *come on*; that was Seln's, mostly. And a hand turned over empty, as a girl had once turned hers over to him on a hillside, was *nothing*: the thing had gone, or it had never been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-190-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md:191:"Stand; seen; come; nothing." Vastin made each of them with his own right hand, in its linen, exactly, like a junior learning the seals. "I have them."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-192-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-193-Thirty yards ahead, at a bend, a small grey figure lifted two fingers.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-194-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-210-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-211-"That's well enough," she said, low. "Now look at yourself. No, don't move. Look where you are."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md-212-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-13.md:213:He was in the middle of the road, upright between the two ruts, with his weight laid evenly on both feet and the stick grounded, as he had stood on a landing in Ostrand and at the head of a ferry's planks.
