editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-20.md:77:"I shall tell you what a catalogue says, and you will remember that it is a catalogue." She did not look at him. "The registry keeps a class that it calls historical studies. It is a small one. The Paths in it are of no use on a floor or in a field, and so nobody has troubled to rank them high; I do not know which of them he has. What they have in common is that they are turned on made things. A wall. A seal. The binding of a book. Such a person can say how a thing was put together: what was laid first, and what rests on what, and whether two things came from one hand."
