85:"Sits. The lot of it sits. There's not an order on that skin from the head to the tail." He straightened. "Somebody's telling you what was done. He's not telling you to do it."
125:"I held that for the whole of my service, and was easy in it. Above Ostrand I was shown that the fault was meant. I called it corrupt; I put down a seal upon that word, and walked three hundred miles on it, and thought that I had come to the floor." The stick's foot turned upon the cobbles. "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-39.md:15:*I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be.*
books/book-08-before-the-paths/chapters/chapter-02.md:143:He had it. He had had it since the landing. He remembered a table in a borrowed office in Ostrand, four streets back from the registry seat, a room with nothing of anyone's in it, and the man in front of him now in grey, and a sentence, said once, after the longest silence he had ever sat through: *I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be.* And then nothing. No alliance, no files, no hand across the table. The man had said the sentence and gone back inside and stayed there, and Cael had carried the sentence across the Line in Hesk's satchel as the only true thing the Compact had ever handed him, and had never once expected to hear the voice that said it again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-40.md:125:"I held that for the whole of my service, and was easy in it. Above Ostrand I was shown that the fault was meant. I called it corrupt; I put down a seal upon that word, and walked three hundred miles on it, and thought that I had come to the floor." The stick's foot turned upon the cobbles. "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-08.md:197:He was the only man within a hundred miles who had ever been such an officer. He stood at the sill in a drover's coat of brown frieze, which was too short in the sleeve and smelled of sheep; he had bought it at the last market inside the Line, and had left a grey one on its hook. He had an ash stick, cut out of a hedge. He had a pack with one strap mended in cord. Under the pack, flat against his back, lay a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather, which he had carried so for three hundred miles less a few. Inside his coat, in a fold of oilcloth, there was a single copied page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-39.md:17:That had cost him a seal, left in a tray on a morning of rain, and three hundred miles on a hedge-stick. He had thought it the end of the matter. A man finds that the scale was made to read false; he lays down his office; he goes to dig up the one buried thing that he has the knowledge to find. He had supposed, on the road, that the thing would turn out to be a fraud. He had been ready for a fraud. He had dealt with a great many.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-21.md:155:It did not. There had been people in his life who had filed him because they were afraid, and each of them had called it procedure to the end. This one had done a right thing, for the reason that he gave. He had then walked three hundred miles on a bad knee and got down on a bank, where he could not rise, to say that he had also been glad of it for a wrong one. Nobody had asked him. Nobody living could have found it out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-10.md:89:"From the Compact's house. It is three hundred miles, by the post road for the first part, and then by a road that has no name."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-10.md:221:"I know that you would, and you are right to. But I have carried it three hundred miles without saying it aloud, and I would have you meet it as it stands on the page before you meet it in my mouth. I am not a witness to what it means. I should only be putting my voice between you and the page."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-10.md:245:Cael saw it happen, and it took him a breath to understand what he was seeing. The man had finished. He had come three hundred miles to say perhaps a dozen sentences at a board, and he had said them before the pot was cold; and his right hand had gone out, a little way, across the wood, to the place where a pen would lie.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-40.md:125:"I held that for the whole of my service, and was easy in it. Above Ostrand I was shown that the fault was meant. I called it corrupt; I put down a seal upon that word, and walked three hundred miles on it, and thought that I had come to the floor." The stick's foot turned upon the cobbles. "Now you're telling me it was *aimed*."

