editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/recheck-r1.md:75:**Protected wording and reserved disclosures — PASS.** The mapped lines are exact, including “You kept my file too, then,” both limit sentences, *Not this either. Still open.*, “It's not evidence. It's a map,” the borrowed-office description, and “I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be.” The Shadow notice remains exact. The older word appears in one chapter only. The Tide anomaly receives only its inventory and non-connection check; no Tide practitioner appears. No forbidden maker, Architect, Quieting, or purpose disclosure is introduced.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:| 40 | The Instrument | 6,764 | 7 | Day 94: Cael proposes Vastin; **worst versions in turn** (Brom, Karis, Lira, Seln, Cael); **Karis's rule, said by all five**; **five hands, Seln's last**. Seln's way in: the posted station closures (the river inspection), the inn on the wharf, the note (*Neither office's. Nothing written.* — Vastin's own Norhold note cut to four words), the borrowed room. Day 98: five ways down; **the borrowed office** (verbatim description; shapes of ledgers in the dust; the cupola); **"Front stair… eleven minutes early."** **The reading** (the father's letter twice; *Continue observation*; his lens on the seals; Karis's gloves for the leaf). **The longest silence.** **"I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be."** **Three refusals** (verify — theater, "runs on the thing it accuses"; report — an oath to a forger; certify — "It is the only sentence I have left that they still need."). **Nine thousand evaluations.** "Are you with us?" / **"No. I am not with anyone."** Thanks the room. **Seln: "He was not managing us."** **Cael: "He didn't join us. I'd have trusted him less if he had."** **VASTIN window (~1,850):** the river stations (a keeper's open drawer of margins he does not touch); the junior's copy out of *held*; the clean margin; every verification gone through and refused (the shim; the reading; the station sheet's ledger line; the junior); the junior at the door — "Continue observation" given to keep him safe; the five not written down; he files nothing, does not write; "Yes"; home at the ordinary hour. |
