editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:76:26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9827:series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:298:**External arc:** The Architect's preserved will completes its activation sequence. Its first observable action: targeted suppression of Fractured Path signatures. Not the Quieting — something more specific. Equipment fails specifically when Cael uses it. Navigation records are corrupted around his location. Practitioners near him begin experiencing interference with their own abilities — not Quieting, but something that seems tied to his presence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:9834:series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:318:**The loss:** One companion — Seln — makes a choice that Cael cannot follow. Not a betrayal. A different decision about what the right path is. Seln believes the Architect's reset, while devastating, may be necessary — that the existing system, built on falsification and suppression, cannot be reformed, only replaced. He is not wrong about the system's corruption. He is not right that the reset is the answer. He leaves the companions to pursue his own response to the Quieting. He is still alive. He is no longer here.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-002/plan-audit.stdout.log:10140:    88	His arc: the man who enforced a corrupt system for legitimate reasons, and what he does when he understands the system is far more corrupt than he knew.
