editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:142:- **The fire, as re-joined (r1).** Lira reads once; Cael turns his face away and watches eight bowls cool; she folds the page and says her line **to the fire**, before anything else; then the hole and the ruled box ("There's a stroke in the hole." / "Yes."); then she puts her thumb on the place through the paper and looks across at him. What her line does to him is told while Brom reads. **Seln (only "I'll keep it a while longer." fixed):** "There is a house on that hill which would give a great deal to have it laid upon its ledge; and I have asked myself on a good many nights what it was that I kept it out of… I had only ever seen that house from the inside of its own books. It stands upon this. I know now what the office is for, which I did not know at noon; and I had rather know it and carry the thing, than carry it blind." No count of years; the case on his chest, shut; nothing in it named. **Cael sits** on the fifth bucket when Seln hands the page back, so that Vastin's "Who's sitting across the fire" is so, and **gets up off it** for pole two. **Vastin's joins:** "I held that for the whole of my service, and was easy in it. Above Ostrand I was shown that the fault was meant. I called it corrupt; I put down a seal upon that word, and walked three hundred miles on it, and thought that I had come to the floor." He lifts his eyes from the fire only for the last piece. Before "I would have.": "He could have left it there, and it would have been true." **Pole two's joins:** "He had breath left for three words." / "It was Lira, and she had not taken her eyes off him since he got up." / "He stopped there, since the rest of it was not a plan."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-006/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:164:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd**; slat-bound; he rides the cart, sleeps in a stall, and takes the inner stair on his seat. He kept silent at the beam after one sentence. He heard the leaf; reached once aloud and was stopped; has stopped the same sentence in his own head; has said his piece at the fire (imperfect; the fault meant, which he called corrupt; aimed) and answered Lira ("I would have."). He was told across a dinner table that out here one counts who is owed a seat. He does not know the mechanism, the eleventh, the twelfth, the sum, or what is under the bar. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it.
