editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-39.md:145:He did not mean to read it. He meant only to see that it was whole. But it had opened a little in his coat, and the first line lay under his thumb in a small upright hand; and his eyes went along that line before he had given them leave.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-39.md:177:Cael had been asked not to say it over, and he did not. He gave it as a carter gives a load to the man who is to take the other shaft: who had put it up, and whom it was meant for.
