   626	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   627	**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and ninety-third day past the Line**, in the long loft at Treswick. Days on the page: 291 (the ladder; the carts' street; the beam; the hatch; the gallery; the inside; the twelfth; the telling; the stair), the night of 291–292 (the tail), 292 (below; the parcel; the meal; the inventory; the light), Oryn at her fourth gate from dusk on the 292nd to first light on the 293rd, 293 (the leaf; the chronicle; the copy; Vastin's afternoon and stair; the street; the yard fire). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
   628	
   629	**Where everyone is.** Five in the loft (Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln at the ladder's head) and Vastin in the end stall beneath. Cleon has gone back up through the blue gate; the leaf, the chronicle and the board are under the registry; the fifty-two sheets lie on their tables one night more. Oryn and the brown mule are between her fourth gate and her fifth. Teague's five are east of the river (not on the page).
   630	
   631	**Cael.** Nineteen. **Twelve fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** The twelfth is acquired, read, told to Cleon, and held shut; three unmeant glances, not counted; never on a person, the crown, the leaf or himself. He keeps Cleon's warning and has told nobody. He has ruled that the twelfth is not turned inward until Oryn has been asked. He has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; one unsteady moment was seen on the loft's boards and entered fourth on the page of the inventory, ruling *hold*. He has stood at the blue gate's groove by night and gone back down. He has heard the leaf, carried its copy, and said pole two aloud on his feet at the fire; it is not in the log. **Vastin is still not told of the eleventh**; the debt is entered as heavier. He owes Oryn two tellings at the mill (the readings round the place; the twelfth). Body: sound; tar on his palms; eyes recovered.
   632	
   633	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. Arm: day twenty-eight out of the wool on the 293rd; it steadied a page and drew a blanket along two nails. Right shoulder still bruised. She was told first and read the page first. She has twice been refused something Cael had no leave to give (the warning; the leaf before the fire) and has said so. She closed the gap by the blanket without looking. Her registry paper is untouched.
   634	
   635	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No grey. Neither arm above the elbow; the box on the bound right shoulder; he was the handcart's horse and brake. He put his thumb to a carrier's slip. **The purse: a hundred and thirty.** He means to buy the rope before the gate. Owed at the mill to two healers.
   636	
   637	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three; no point struck since the fork (she did not light the yard fire). **All twenty-three letters.** She has read the first face of the leaf aloud once, given one account of it, shown Vastin's copied page to Cleon, marked one line of the chronicle and not read on, and made two copies with the gap ruled as an empty box and the one stroke drawn. She has kept two pages in the chamber and at the fire. She has not gone into the leaf's back (a list). Left palm: stitches in, under linen; she has begun to use the hand without noticing.
   638	
