+# Verdict: CLOSE
+
+The repaired manuscript closes with no line fixes. I read the full current Movement 6 (chapters 34–40), compared every changed region with `pre-repair-r1/` using `diff -U0`, checked the closed edition and Movement 7 inheritance, opened the five named source passages, and ran the required formula, overlap, gate and sweep commands. The repair resolves every brief item; the protected text is whole, once, and on the right speaker; and no repaired join creates a continuity or source-tracking failure.
+
+Three descriptions in the latest `STATE_LEDGER.md` remain stale after the repair, but they are record housekeeping rather than manuscript faults: line 639 retains Seln's removed “largest thing” claim and calls his sentence marker 11; line 641 still calls Vastin's pieces markers 12–13; and line 655 still says “Sixteen markers.” The surviving speech at `manuscript/chapter-40.md:87` contains no “largest thing” claim, and the movement contains zero `{{JOIN}}` and zero `[[TIER-B` markers. None of the binding bullets in `LEDGER-RULINGS.md` is unsupported by the prose.
+
+## (1) Brief items
+
+The evidence below is from the zero-context diff against `state/movement-006/pre-repair-r1/`; a quoted line prefixed by `+` is repair text. Items whose required words were already in the coordinator-applied baseline are checked in the surviving text as well.
+
+### A. Ruled material kept
+
+1. **RESOLVED — the twelfth remains unbidden and outward.** No repair reverses the settled behavior. The revised inward-test chain ends with `+*Write it down and stop touching it.*` and `+*Not until she's heard it*` (`chapter-35.md:107,111`), so the one inward test is refused. The movement's outward looks remain the chamber/board, rope-walk, bridge, handcart hinge, dividers and inn table. The twelfth is never turned inward, on a person, the crown or the leaf.
+2. **RESOLVED — the chronicle stands as ruled.** The repair leaves the spoken line, the hole and Karis's refusal intact: “I am not going to read into a hole,” followed by Karis's “Marked.” and Cleon's “Marked.” (`chapter-38.md:197–215`). Nobody glosses the hole or speaks of the line again.
+3. **RESOLVED — *The Architect* remains spoken once.** It occurs once, spoken by Karis at `chapter-38.md:147`; the restored clause is exactly “It's a title, not a name; the name's gone.” at line 153.
+4. **RESOLVED — all thirteen author flags remain kept.** The weigh-beam is charged to Cleon's card; Vastin rides, sleeps in the stall and takes the inner stair on his seat; *and* / *set* remain Karis's letter facts; Seln's slip remains opaque; the beyond-Line Kindling remains Oryn's isolated cutaway; the leaf audiences remain separated; the watcher has no face, name or base; Cleon's extra day remains; and the accepted length is 36,152 words.
+
+### B. Coordinator-applied protected text and joins
+
+1. **RESOLVED — Cleon's three pieces.** The repair supplies short, edition-native elaboration between the fixed units: `+"A load came in at a gate... There's not a mark on that leaf that's waiting for anything."` and `+"Whoever cut this set each sign where it is for the sake of the one after it... I'm walked down it."` (`chapter-35.md:15–31`). The order is “A record ... sits.” / “An instruction *leans*.” / “This is a stair.”; no *bearer* appears.
+2. **RESOLVED — “There,” lands at the row's end.** The diff adds `+above the last sign of the run it stopped`, followed by Cleon's “There,” and “It came at that word.” (`chapter-35.md:47–51`). The pronoun's antecedent is the new fragment/acquisition, not the finger or the row.
+3. **RESOLVED — Cleon's refusal is whole.** “No. I'll not say that one. Not down here. Not to you.” remains once, Cleon's, at `chapter-35.md:225`.
+4. **RESOLVED — the warning has its two joins.** The repair places Cleon at the third table speaking to the oak, then adds `+The reed lay along the table's edge...` and `+He stopped. The square finger had come off the reed.` (`chapter-35.md:237–247`). All three protected spoken pieces remain whole.
+5. **RESOLVED — the cups line is Cael's and addressed to Vastin.** The added bridge says `+He had said it across the table, to the one person at it who had audited seats for a registry` (`chapter-37.md:197`); Vastin answers at line 199.
+6. **RESOLVED — both halves of the leaf are whole.** The first join is only Karis taking breath at a comma (`chapter-38.md:109`). At the scraped place she leaves the record's words, states in her own voice that four or five letters are gone and one stroke remains, then resumes the protected second half (`chapter-38.md:111–119`). No leaf wording is omitted or transferred to another speaker.
+7. **RESOLVED — title clause.** The diff adds a pencil movement into the exact protected sentence, “It's a title, not a name; the name's gone.” (`chapter-38.md:151–153`).
+8. **RESOLVED — “Older ... Made. Us.”** Karis's three words remain whole and once at `chapter-38.md:167`.
